        <mxCell id="XOWEwEKvRYx0S_CinpEg-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article-box__container-title u-h3 js-expandable-title&quot; id=&quot;Sec5&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; line-height: 1.4rem; box-sizing: inherit; margin-bottom: 8px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Box 1 Binding motif databases and motif matcher algorithms&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Inferences&lt;/b&gt;: bulk Expr;&amp;nbsp; TF binding and bulk chromatin accessibility; Single-cell transcriptomics data&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Downstream GRN analyses:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Topological analysis (&lt;b&gt;network centrality&lt;/b&gt;, TF drive cell fate changes in diverse biological contexts; &lt;b&gt;spectral graph theory, GRN as a matrix, non-negative matrix factorization to find groups of TFs with certain functionality&lt;/b&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Comparative analysis (to identify &lt;b&gt;rewiring events different from cell types, states, etc.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Inference of TF activities (+ gene expression into TF topology to infer which TF to have relevant role in certain contexts. Enrichment).&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-022-05060-x&quot;&gt;Spatial multi-omic map of human myocardial infarction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Perturbation and prediction of cell fate ()&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Experimental assessment of GRNs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*TF abundance and post-translational modification (Transcripts are a proxy of protein abundance, let alone activity; single-cell proteomics is still challenging, but spatial proteomics is possible but costly.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*TF binding and cooperativity&amp;nbsp; (&lt;b&gt;TF assigned to the chromatin regions&lt;/b&gt; based on its binding motif. However, TF motif may have low specificity, so &lt;b&gt;ChIP-seq&lt;/b&gt; data are necessary as it provide more accurate binding info than motif.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Regulatory activity of CREs ( three states: active, poised or repressive. &lt;b&gt;MPRA, CRISPR-based perturbation&lt;/b&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Linkage to target genes&amp;nbsp; (HiC, gene regulation based on sustained genomic interactions, )&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-family: monospace; font-size: 0px; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;%3CmxGraphModel%3E%3Croot%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%222%22%20parent%3D%221%22%20style%3D%22shape%3Dimage%3BverticalLabelPosition%3Dbottom%3BlabelBackgroundColor%3Ddefault%3BverticalAlign%3Dtop%3Baspect%3Dfixed%3BimageAspect%3D0%3Bimage%3Ddata%3Aimage%2Fpng%2CiVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAABIAAAAKOCAIAAABREPVHAAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAgAElEQVR4nOzdeZxUxbU48HNO1b3dM%2By7Am7RKAquuBD3vASfK6CIiJjFJYmRuCSaF0OMz%2BTFJCZqFpOoIaK4REHcF9T4M7iBghLRyKqCKJsg68x0971V5%2Fz%2BqO6eHpgBNQzLzPl%2B%2BjMM3T33Vt%2Fe6txTdQpFBJRSSimllFJKNT%2Fa1g1QSimllFJKqdZCAzCllFJKKaWU2ko0AFNKKaWUUkqprcRu6wYopdQW0sSEVkYAACrf6sV7FARrAQgKADUA6wE%2BLMALr%2Benv%2FPeh6vWz3p3QWHtWrAW6mfJiiHqu%2B%2BePXfq2Gf3nY49eOe%2BXaE9QBagGiBiQADwCUThrBaCEEjYMTBA8XTXpqfc4pY5DEoppZTanqEW4VBKtRBNfJh5BAAwUh%2FhCIAHyAE4gMXr4d5HJj8%2BedqStYU6iCHb3rTp4NFks9nKj0cUcIW8NVKzbqXhXMblumbNwCMOO%2Fm4I7%2FUr101QBYAPRgjAFwKwAAAgEAAws5RAzCllFKq1dMATCnVUjT6YYbgAEoJKBYED%2BQAagCem1U75v7H3pm7sMaRbds5bt8xQaE4w0hIxnvPwpGNSpsBcczsGHw2Y9PaGs7VSS7HuZpde3S66JzBZx3TszNABGCB66OvkAzDyuZsqqlKKaWUavE0AFNKtRRNB2ACQAAeIAXIA%2Fxz5uJ7Hn%2F%2B%2BX9%2F6LJdqtp2MnF1CuQJwUIhLQiLsdalaVV1lXO%2BtBkgIBZ24gFAvM9GsWV0%2BbradZ%2FY3Kp9u2RHjRh0xnF7VQPEIe